            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MORAWAJ"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Al, I joined my recipes to specifically write a review of your cocktail sauce. I have tried making a handfull of highly rated cocktail sauce recipes I found all over the net, but I MUST say that I preferred yours the most. It tastes great and is EXTREMELY easy to make! To boot it only has 4 ingredients, which everyone will most likely have on hand. The exception is the fresh horseradish. So, I used about 1.25 - 1.5 teaspoons of prepared white horseradish which suited my tastes just fine. Great job, keep em coming!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Betty Dickson"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I tripled the recipe because I like to have extra. I did cut way back on the horseradish as I like it but seeing how much that was called for made me wary. I mixed the other ingredients together first and added prepared horseradish by the teaspoon until it tasted right. I'm guessing the tablespoons that it called for should have been teaspoons instead because I like horseradish a lot and that would have been way too much. I also added some granulated garlic powder for a bit more flavor. I also decided it need a bit of saltiness and added Tajin, a spice I try to always have in my cupboard. It is a spicy lime type salty spice. I really will make this recipe from now on, with my changes of course.",
            "datePublished": "2020-10-04T22:39:44.637Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "binanndunn"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Absolutely awesome - clean, astringent, full-flavored. As noted in other reviews, that little bit of brown sugar is what makes this recipe turn the corner. Again, as noted elsewhere, all I had on hand was (good quality) prepared horseradish (grated horseradish/vinegar NOT horseradish cream or salad dressing) I used a scant two table spoons and probably 1/4 teaspoon lemon (cut a lemon into wedges, used 1 wedge to flavor the sauce). I will never, ever, ever, buy the bottled stuff again. First class!",
            "datePublished": "2012-02-22T16:47:26.027Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SColv"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used prepared horseradish (genuinely not sure if raw horseradish is something different that I should be able to find in the store, but I didn't investigate and just used what I had) and got rave reviews. It was perfect and tasted exactly how I'd expected/ hoped!",
            "datePublished": "2022-01-02T13:39:39.023Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
