            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "sherby61"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a good recipe,but we've always made our own sauce and we also add about 2 to 3 tsp Worcestershire sauce and chili sauce for extra kick. Don't think we have ever bought prepared cocktail sauce. Such an easy thing to make. Don't know why people waste money paying for it when you usually always have these items on hand anyways.",
            "datePublished": "2014-01-21T00:12:30.410Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jim"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent, better than store bought. Outa ketchup so I had to sub chili sauce and added an extra tablespoon of brown sugar to compensate for lost sugar in ketchup. So good!!",
            "datePublished": "2024-01-20T20:40:20.002Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "TxCin2"
            },
            "reviewBody": "It easier than I thought to make cocktail sauce. I used a grated horseradish in the jar for this. It didn't look quite like the bottled cocktail sauce, but it was rated \"better than any bottled sauce I've EVER eaten\". I used this for peel and eat shrimp as a dipping sauce. This would be simple to modify to your heat tolerance/preference by adjusting the amount of horseradish. We're definitely making this again.",
            "datePublished": "2026-05-09T01:43:20.025Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
